{"repositoryId":1214524747,"availability":"available","full":"ch0wm3in/psst-secret","name":"psst-secret","description":"A secure secret sharing platform","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-18T17:38:17Z","updated":"2026-10-15T15:01:17Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://psst-secret-1-1-4.onrender.com/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:46.726Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:46.726Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:46.726Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:46.726Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A privacy-focused, zero-knowledge app for sharing secrets securely. We call them whispers. All encryption and decryption happens in the browser — the server never sees your plaintext. By default, encrypted data and public key material are stored only in volatile memory (Redis with persistence disabled) and never touch disk.","The fragment is the part of a URL after #. RFC 3986 §3.5 reserves it for browser-side processing, and RFC 9110 §7.1 excludes it from HTTP requests. Key material in the fragment is therefore not sent to the server or included in HTTP request logs. Password-protected view links contain no decryption key fragment."],"features":["Zero-knowledge architecture — whispers are encrypted client-side with AES-256-GCM using the Web Crypto API. Decryption key material stays in the view link's URL fragment or is protected by your password.","In-memory ciphertext storage — encrypted data and public key material are stored in Redis with persistence disabled (--save \"\" --appendonly no) by default. Ciphertexts never touch disk in this configuration. If Redis…","Send mode — encrypt a whisper (text or file) and get a shareable link.","Receive mode — create a request using X-Wing, a hybrid of ML-KEM-768 (post-quantum, FIPS 203) and X25519. Share a submit link containing the public-key fingerprint and keep a separate view link containing the private…","Post-quantum ready — send mode uses 256-bit symmetric encryption; receive mode uses hybrid key exchange, which remains protected as long as either component holds."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ch0wm3in/psst-secret/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"706238d5939f61de5ed605740a0cfea59c2efff8d4a52eb1202e5e7479ad3642","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:46.879Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:46.879Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A privacy-focused, zero-knowledge app for sharing secrets securely. We call them whispers. All encryption and decryption happens in the browser — the server never sees your plaintext. By default, encrypted data and public key material are stored only in volatile memory (Redis with persistence disabled) and never touch disk.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ch0wm3in/psst-secret/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"optional","text":"Deployment summary — the About page lists which optional features and sign-in requirements are enabled on the instance, in plain language for end users.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ch0wm3in/psst-secret/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Additional readers must already have active accounts with unique, verified primary email addresses in django-allauth.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ch0wm3in/psst-secret/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"706238d5939f61de5ed605740a0cfea59c2efff8d4a52eb1202e5e7479ad3642","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ch0wm3in/psst-secret/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:46.880Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T15:01:17Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ch0wm3in/psst-secret/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:46.881Z","hash":"706238d5939f61de5ed605740a0cfea59c2efff8d4a52eb1202e5e7479ad3642","originalBytes":34645,"storedBytes